{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517536-dilettante-and-jack-of-all-trades","id":1517536,"title":"Dilettante and Jack-of-All-Trades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-08T21:13:40-07:00","id":1517536,"title":"Dilettante and Jack-of-All-Trades","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused on the effect of these two merits, the questions would be:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>By getting <b>Dilettante </b>at 3 pt. do you also get the effects of the 1 pt. version?</li> <li>Mechanically, is it worthwhile to have <b>Jack-of-All-Trades</b> and <b>Dilettante </b>3?\u200b</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T09:11:17-07:00","id":1517567,"title":"","content":"Dilettante (introduced in <b>The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b>, p.44) lets you perform untrained skills without penalty at level 1, and lets you gain an automatic success on a complementary roll or an untrained skill roll. As a general role of thumb, I view multi-level Merits as stacking their effects; so yes, I'd say that three dots of Dilettante should provide both benefits.<br /> <br /> Jack-of-all-Trades (<b>Book of Secrets</b> p.45) lets you attempt untrained skills without the +1 difficulty, <i>and</i> lets you attempt untrained Knowledges, albeit at +2 difficulty. There's some overlap, in that Joat includes the benefits of the first level of Dilettante; but that automatic success that the third level provides is worthwhile in its own right. I'd have no problem allowing both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-10-2023, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T08:16:20-07:00","id":1517650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517536-dilettante-and-jack-of-all-trades?p=1517567#post1517567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dilettante (introduced in <b>The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b>, p.44) lets you perform untrained skills without penalty at level 1, and lets you gain an automatic success on a complementary roll or an untrained skill roll. As a general role of thumb, I vote multi-level Merits as attacking their effects; so yes, I'd say that three dots of Dilettante should provide both benefits.<br /> <br /> Jack-of-all-Trades (<b>Book of Secrets</b> p.45) lets you attempt untrained skills without the +1 difficulty, <i>and</i> lets you attempt untrained Knowledges, albeit at +2 difficulty. There's some overlap, in that Joat includes the benefits of the first level of Dilettante; but that automatic success that the third level provides is worthwhile in its own right. I'd have no problem allowing both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, this is what I was thinking, but wanted some confirmation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}